Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: minti-status
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
 minti-cland
Description: MINTI live terminal-UI status dashboard
 Continuously-refreshing terminal dashboard for a MINTI node. Surfaces
 local Clan membership (who is in the Clan, who is Orchestrator, recent
 failovers), runtime + currently-loaded LLM (via minti-runtime + Ollama
 /api/ps), installed addon packs, and the configured agent harness
 (opencode + optional Claude Code preset).
 .
 Read-only in v1 (M7) — no mutations from the UI. Three independent
 refresh tickers (2s / 5s / 30s) keep the dashboard live without blocking
 the UI on any single probe. Keybinds: q quit, r force refresh, ?/h help.
 .
 Run with `minti-status` for the interactive view, or `minti-status --once`
 to print a single snapshot to stdout (e.g. piping into a journal entry
 or running under SSH non-TTY). The `--no-color` flag (also via NO_COLOR
 env) disables ANSI escapes.
 .
 Ships a pre-built Go binary (compiled by `make status-linux` on the host
 or in CI) at /usr/bin/minti-status. Recommends minti-cland because the
 Clan panel — the headline — needs the cland CLI on PATH to shell out.
